@@ -4,6 +4,11 @@ Changelog
 *unreleased*
 ~~~~~~~~~~~~
 
+Features:
+
+* Add ``Requirement.__replace__`` for validated copies with selected fields
+  changed, including support for ``copy.replace()`` on Python 3.13 and later.
+
 Removals:
 
 * Drop support for EOL Python 3.9. (:pull:`1263`)
diff --git a/docs/requirements.rst b/docs/requirements.rst
index fede671..28d632f 100644
--- a/docs/requirements.rst
+++ b/docs/requirements.rst
@@ -60,6 +60,20 @@ Usage
     >>> requirements2 = {Requirement("pip"), Requirement("packaging")}
     >>> requirements1 == requirements2
     True
+    >>> req.__replace__(name="other", extras={"test"})
+    <Requirement('other[test]<3,>=2; python_version > "2.0"')>
+
+Use ``Requirement.__replace__`` to create a new requirement with selected fields
+changed. It accepts the keyword arguments ``name``, ``url``, ``extras``,
+``specifier``, and ``marker``, with the same types as the corresponding
+attributes. On Python 3.13 and later, ``copy.replace(req, name="other")`` also
+works. Unknown fields raise :exc:`TypeError`; invalid values or combinations
+raise :exc:`InvalidRequirement`.
+
+Unspecified fields are retained. The new requirement is parsed and normalized,
+and its specifier set and individual specifiers are independent copies that
+preserve explicit prerelease settings. Subclasses are constructed through their
+initializer.
 
 .. versionchanged:: 23.2
 
